{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.Mass.ColorCurveSheets","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.Mass.ColorCurveSheets","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:QOU.Mass.ColorCurveQPartials"],"declarations":2,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.ColorCurveSheets.defect_eq_shifted_sheet_product","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.ColorCurveSheets.defect_eq_shifted_sheet_product","kind":"theorem","line":60,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/ColorCurveSheets.lean#L60-L69","doc":"**The defect is the product of gaps to the shifted sheets.** On `Σ` (`C_z(X)=0`), if\n`Y₁,Y₂,Y₃` are the sheets over the shifted base `qz` (`C_{qz}(Y)=∏(Y−Yᵢ)` at `Y=X`), then\nthe q-shift defect is `Δ_q^z C(X,z) = (X−Y₁)(X−Y₂)(X−Y₃)`. Thus the branch is coherent\n(defect `0`) iff `X` equals one shifted sheet; selecting that sheet is the branch datum\n`D_q` must provide. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.ColorCurveSheets.colorCubic_from_sheets","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.ColorCurveSheets.colorCubic_from_sheets","kind":"theorem","line":46,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/ColorCurveSheets.lean#L46-L58","doc":"**Vieta reconstruction.** If `X₁,X₂,X₃` are the three sheets over `z` — i.e. their\nelementary symmetric functions are the (q-integer) coefficients of `C_z` — then they\nreconstruct the curve: `(X−X₁)(X−X₂)(X−X₃) = C_z(X)`. The sheets are governed collectively\nby the q-integer symmetric functions; branch selection breaks this S₃ symmetry. ","signatureChunk":0}]}